---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Support — GPS-Go';
const description = 'Support and contact for GPS-Go by Yaner Apps.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} currentPath="/support/">
  <div class="prose">
    <div class="prose-header">
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">Questions, bug reports, and privacy requests for GPS-Go.</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <span>Updated: 21 Sep 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:yanerapps@gmail.com">yanerapps@gmail.com</a>. To help us reproduce a
      problem, please include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your device model and Android version</li>
      <li>The app version (Settings &rarr; About)</li>
      <li>What you did, what you expected, and what happened instead</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Common questions</h2>

    <h3>The app says it is not the selected mock location app</h3>
    <p>
      Android requires you to pick a mock location app in Developer options. Open
      <strong>Settings &rarr; System &rarr; Developer options &rarr; Select mock location app</strong> and choose GPS-Go.
      If Developer options is not visible, go to <strong>Settings &rarr; About phone</strong> and tap <strong>Build number</strong> 7 times to unlock it.
      The in-app setup checklist walks you through this and the other permissions.
    </p>

    <h3>Simulation stops when the screen is off or app is in background</h3>
    <p>
      Android's power management may terminate background services to save battery. Go to
      <strong>Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr; GPS-Go &rarr; Battery</strong> (or <strong>App battery usage</strong>) and select <strong>Unrestricted</strong>.
      You can also open this setting from the in-app setup checklist.
    </p>

    <h3>Some apps still show my real location</h3>
    <p>
      Apps that verify location integrity, or that read location through their own means, can detect or
      ignore a mocked position. GPS-Go feeds the standard Android location providers; it cannot guarantee
      that every third-party app will accept the simulated position.
    </p>

    <h3>The floating joystick does not appear</h3>
    <p>
      The joystick needs the "Display over other apps" permission. Grant it from the in-app setup checklist
      or from <strong>Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr; GPS-Go &rarr; Display over other apps</strong>.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I change my ad consent choice?</h3>
    <p>
      In the app, go to <strong>Settings &rarr; About &rarr; Privacy Options</strong>. This entry appears where
      consent applies. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for details.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I delete my data?</h3>
    <p>
      All data is stored on your device and can be deleted in the app. Uninstalling GPS-Go removes
      everything.
    </p>

    <h2>Responsible use</h2>
    <p>
      GPS-Go simulates the location of your own device, for testing, development, and privacy purposes. Do
      not use it to deceive other people or to violate the terms of any service you use. You are
      responsible for how you use it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
